      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 12,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Pick your own files\n\nBoth of these ship with nothing chosen, because a checkpoint name off my\nmachine would just be a red node on yours.\n\nChoose any two checkpoints you have. They do not have to be related - the\nmore different they are, the more obvious the comparison.\n\nEach loader's MODEL, CLIP and VAE go to a different switcher. That is the\nwhole point of this file: the three parts are being routed separately, on\npurpose.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        400,
        590
      ],
      "size": [
        300,
        280
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 13,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Three switchers, one axis\n\nRow 1 is checkpoint A, row 2 is checkpoint B.\n\nTick both rows on all three and you get two runs. Tick row 1 only and you\nget one run - and **B never loads**.\n\nThe trap: these do not multiply each other. 3 models plus 2 VAEs is three\nruns, not six, because ComfyUI zips the lists rather than crossing them.\nRead the big note for the full story, and use **EPS Run Multiplier**\n(`models` -> `model`, `vaes` -> `vae`; its default `sweep_mode: multiply`\ndoes the crossing) when you genuinely want every combination.\n\nIf all three pieces come from the same file anyway, EPS Checkpoint Switcher\nis the node you want instead.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
